  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that changes the $1$st  row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =[\\begin{aligned}60 & 0 & 120 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}] & \\,{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}.\n$$",
